WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.010
In 1859, Charles Darwin ended his most
famous book with a sentence full of wonder.

2
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.730
All life, he wrote,
began from a few forms,

3
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.340
or from one.

4
00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:17.310
From so simple a beginning came
endless forms most beautiful.

5
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.070
Genesis says God formed man
from the dust of the ground,

6
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.290
and breathed life into him.

7
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:27.920
So if humans evolved from earlier life,
can they still be made in the image of

8
00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:29.160
God?

9
00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.490
In this mission, you'll see
how natural selection works,

10
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.710
and the evidence scientists
point to: fossils,

11
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.920
anatomy and DNA.

12
00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:42.340
Then you'll find out why Christians
disagree so sharply about what it means for

13
00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.530
humans.

14
00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:48.850
Your mission: weigh up whether evolved
humans can still be made in God's image.
